Simon's algorithm for f(x) = f(x XOR s) with n = 3 and secret s = 110.
Qubits 0-2 hold x, qubits 3-5 hold f(x). The oracle copies x into the
second register, then (since s_0 = 1) XORs x_0 into every y_j with
s_j = 1. Each run's outcome y satisfies y . s = 0 (mod 2).
